a": "web"}}, {"t": 571, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "-store"}}, {"t": 572, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "`"}}, {"t": 573, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": " on"}}, {"t": 574, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": " the"}}, {"t": 575, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": " same"}}, {"t": 577, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": " node"}}, {"t": 577, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "."}}, {"t": 579, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "  \n"}}, {"t": 580, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "[k"}}, {"t": 581, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "ubernetes"}}, {"t": 582, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": ":s"}}, {"t": 583, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "cheduling"}}, {"t": 584, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "-"}}, {"t": 586, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "ev"}}, {"t": 587, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "iction"}}, {"t": 588, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "/"}}, {"t": 589, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "assign"}}, {"t": 590, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "-p"}}, {"t": 591, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "od"}}, {"t": 592, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "-node"}}, {"t": 593, "type": "llm.token", "data": {"delta": "]"}}, {"t": 595, "type": "gate.citations", "data": {"passed": true, "cited": ["kubernetes:scheduling-eviction/assign-pod-node"], "invented": [], "said_not_in_docs": false}}, {"t": 595, "type": "answer", "data": {"text": "Add a pod\u2011anti\u2011affinity rule that matches the app\u2019s label and uses the node\u2011hostname topology key.  \nExample:\n\n```yaml\nspec:\n  affinity:\n    podAntiAffinity:\n      requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:\n      - labelSelector:\n          matchExpressions:\n          - key: app\n            operator: In\n            values:\n            - web-store\n        topologyKey: \"kubernetes.io/hostname\"\n```\n\nThis tells the scheduler to avoid placing two Pods with `app=web-store` on the same node.  \n[kubernetes:scheduling-eviction/assign-pod-node]", "citations": [{"n": 1, "tag": "kubernetes:scheduling-eviction/assign-pod-node", "source": "kubernetes", "doc": "scheduling-eviction/assign-pod-node.md", "lines": "L497-532", "passages": ["rule tells the scheduler never to place\nmultiple `app=web-store` servers on a single node.\n\n```yaml\napiVersion: apps/v1\nkind: Deployment\nmetadata:\n  name: web-server\nspec:\n  selector:\n    matchLabels:\n      app: web-store\n  replicas: 3\n  template:\n    metadata:\n      labels:\n        app: web-store\n    spec:\n      affinity:\n        podAntiAffinity:\n          requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:\n          - labelSelector:\n              matchExpressions:\n              - key: app\n                operator: In\n                values:\n                - web-store\n            topologyKey: \"kubernetes.io/hostname\"\n        podAffinity:\n          requiredDuringSchedulingIgnoredDuringExecution:\n          - labelSelector:\n              matchExpressions:\n              - key: app\n      ", "in the same defined topology; for example, preferring to place two related\nPods onto the same node.\n\nFor example: imagine a three-node cluster. You use the cluster to run a web application\nand also an in-memory cache (such as Redis). For this example, also assume that latency between\nthe web application and the memory cache should be as low as is practical. You could use inter-pod\naffinity and anti-affinity to co-locate the web servers with the cache as much as possible.\n\nIn the following example Deployment for the Redis cache, the replicas get the label `app=store`. The\n`podAntiAffinity` rule tells the scheduler to avoid placing multiple replicas\nwith the `app=store` label on a single node. This creates each cache in a\nseparate node."], "url": "https://github.com/kubernetes/website/blob/00ace9cad04f8c65259fce8c810d3b4440ded9c6/content/en/docs/concepts/scheduling-eviction/assign-pod-node.md"}]}}, {"t": 595, "type": "done", "data": {"ms_total": 594.8, "llm_ms": 543.0, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 264, "prompt_tokens": 1051, "total_tokens": 1315, "completion_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 131}, "queue_time": 0.117777247, "prompt_time": 0.061513613, "completion_time": 0.279858084, "total_time": 0.341371697}, "ratelimit": {"limit-requests": "1000", "limit-tokens": "8000", "remaining-requests": "991", "remaining-tokens": "4054", "reset-requests": "12m57.599s", "reset-tokens": "29.595s"}}}]}